                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Disclaimer: Special thanks to the developer [url=https://store.steampowered.com/search/?developer=GamePhase]GamePhase[/url] for providing me the key and the opportunity to explore and give an honest review of their challenging little platformer.\n\n\nPixel Art: 3/5......(Not bad for as tiny as the sprites are)\nImmersion: 3/5....(It keeps you coming back for more) \nGameplay: 3/5.....(Nice, simple & clean mechanics) \nControls: 3/5.....(Pretty tight) \nValue: 3.5/5........(Cheap, but also short)\nDifficulty: 3.5/5...(Can be tough to 100%) \n--------------\nOverall 3.1 (Difficulty always excluded)\n\n\nThis is definitely not for everyone...It is close to tough as nails and will appeal mostly to the diehard platformers.\n\nIt is very simple graphic design, but surprising fluid animation for the tiny sprites.\n\nChallenging level design, with a little bit of back and forth that can be annoying.  It can definitely also frustrate in a positive way.\n\nI particularly liked the unique level design, having the baddies behavior contribute significantly to how you progress.\n\nIt is quite gratifying when you do finish a level :)\n\n\nACHIEVEMENTS:  Very tough to 100% this one...There is not only time trial per level, no damage per level, but time trial & no death for entire game :p\n",
